                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>At 11 a.m. Korean time, May 13, 1953, the UNC made its counterproposal at
                    Panmunjom. The record of the session and the text of the proposal can be found
                    in telegrams ZX 36559 and C 62385, both from Clark to JCS, both dated May 13,
                    1953, neither printed. (Matthews files, lot 53 D 413) A text of the UNC
                    counterproposal is printed in the Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, May 25, 1953, pages 755–757.</p>
                <p>At the next session, held May 14, the Communist Delegate stated that the UNC
                    proposal was “absolutely unacceptable” and “resolutely” rejected it. A record of
                    this session can be found in telegram ZX 36570, from Clark to JCS, May 14, 1953.
                    (Matthews files, lot 53 D 413)</p>
            </div>
